### =====================================================================
### notification-service - ready-to-run requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8111, so we send the X-User-* headers ourselves.
###
### Notifications come from events: run e2e/phase7-order-saga.http or e2e/mvp-order-flow.http first
### (or any other flow) and the users below will have notifications.
### Emails: http://localhost:8025 (Mailpit).
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8111


### 1. CUSTOMER (user 4): my notifications, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 2. CUSTOMER (user 4): only the unread ones
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications?unreadOnly=true&size=5
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 3. CUSTOMER (user 4): the badge number
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/unread-count
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 4. CUSTOMER (user 4): mark notification 1 as read (404 if it is not mine)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/1/read
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 5. CUSTOMER (user 7): someone else's notification -> 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/1/read
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 6. VENDOR (user 3, Fresh Mart): new orders, cancellations, low stock
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 7. VENDOR (user 3): mark everything as read
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/read-all
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 8. VENDOR (user 3): badge is 0 now
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/unread-count
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 9. ADMIN: everything the platform sent, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 10. ADMIN: emails that could not be sent
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?emailStatus=FAILED
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 11. ADMIN: all "new order" messages to vendors
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?type=NEW_ORDER
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 12. ADMIN: unknown type -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?type=SMS
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 13. Without the gateway header -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications
